  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "MLX-PROFILE-IMPL-01",
      "severity": "P2",
      "acceptance_blocking": true,
      "title": "The production conftest import graph initializes MLX before profile routing and preflight",
      "location": {
        "path": "tests/conftest.py",
        "line": 24
      },
      "affected_contracts": [
        {
          "plan_field": "decision.default",
          "quote": "They never import/probe MLX just because it happens to be installed."
        },
        {
          "plan_field": "collection_and_hook_design.package_initializers",
          "quote": "The profile guard promises no native backend/test-module import before preflight"
        }
      ],
      "observed": "On the exact d3dcf059 source with plugin autoload disabled and actual MLX installed, unprofiled tests --collect-only succeeds with 1431 core cases and no native test modules, but imports 36 mlx backend modules after 29 backend spec lookups. Canonical native --pyargs correctly exits 4 with the scoped selector diagnostic and no native test-module import, after loading those same backend modules. The integrated alternate and bare --pyargs routes likewise prevent test-module import but initialize the backend first.",
      "cause": "Before pytest_configure can register the profile plugin, tests/conftest.py imports tests.test_utils.fakes. Importing clients.strategies loads its defaults and algorithms.registry. The exact-source trace reaches fedavg_personalized -> serialization.safetensor -> utils.tree:29, which imports mlx.core at module load. algorithms.registry:18 imports mlx_fedavg (which imports the native trainer), and models.registry:26 also eagerly imports the native MLX model. These runtime imports predate this profile commit, but the new accepted profile promise requires their absence from default/preflight-free import paths.",
      "impact": "The safe directory boundary works for native test modules, but default core collection and deliberately rejected native selectors still initialize the optional native backend outside its prerequisite boundary. An independent backend import sentinel demonstrates that such an import failure aborts ordinary core collection as a conftest import error before the intended policy can act. The current working MLX environment passing core tests does not establish the stronger accepted isolation contract.",
      "reproduction": {
        "python": "/tmp/plato-mlx-integration/env/bin/python",
        "cwd": "/tmp/plato-refresh-worktrees/mlx-profile",
        "environment": {
          "PYTHONPATH": "/tmp/plato-refresh-worktrees/mlx-profile",
          "PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD": "1",
          "PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE": "1"
        },
        "runner": "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/import_audit_runner.py",
        "default_arguments": [
          "tests",
          "--collect-only",
          "-p",
          "no:cacheprovider",
          "-q"
        ],
        "canonical_arguments": [
          "--pyargs",
          "tests.mlx_native.test_phase3_controls",
          "-p",
          "no:cacheprovider",
          "-q"
        ]
      },
      "evidence": [
        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/profile-installed-default-audit.json",
        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/profile-installed-default-audit.log",
        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/profile-canonical-pyargs-audit.json",
        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/profile-canonical-pyargs-audit.log",
        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/profile-first-import-trace.log",
