        "/tmp/plato-mlx-profile-independent-review/actual-bare-pyargs-audit.json"
      ],
      "requested_change": "If retaining the accepted contract, make the MLX frontdoors reached by ordinary shared imports lazy, particularly the shared tree utility and model/algorithm registries, without adding a blanket import suppressor, profile bypass, or general optional-backend framework. Add a regression exercising the complete production conftest/module import graph with MLX present or an import sentinel; copied hooks alone cannot cover this failure. A wording-only adjustment would narrow the accepted default/preflight guarantee and therefore needs an explicit reviewed plan revision; it cannot be silently substituted for the existing promise.",
      "severity_rationale": "Normal collection and the native-test directory guard work in the current environment; this is a concrete accepted-contract failure and uncovered dependency initialization, not an observed failure of all native tests or a newly introduced generic runtime import regression. P2 is appropriate, and profile acceptance remains gated on correction or an explicitly revised contract."
    }
  ],
